%S A180206 1,2,4,8,18,56,206,866,3662,16304,77448,405594,2296514,13989280,
%T A180206 89990314,612195224,4379508168,33039187452,261553618840,2171808605286,
%U A180206 18838224530962,170531561222304,1606250624929548,15740000714297474,160065864659464904,1688253382074096582
%N A180206 Number of permutations of 0..(n-1) representable as consecutive sums of 3 adjacent elements of a sequence of n+2 nonnegative integers.
%H A180206 Carlo Corti, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24361784">Counting Permutations of Consecutive Triple Sums: OEIS A180206 through n=26</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%F A180206 From _Carlo Corti_, Nov 19 2026: (Start)
%F A180206 For a finite set S of positive integers, let k = |S| and let F(S) count the orderings (v(1),...,v(k)) of S for which x(j) >= 0 for 1 <= j <= k, where x(-1) = x(0) = 0 and x(j) = v(j) - x(j-1) - x(j-2). Set F({}) = 1.
%F A180206 a(n) = Sum_{S subseteq U} F(S)*F(U \ S), where U = {1,...,n-1}, for n >= 1.
%F A180206 a(n+1) >= 2*a(n), and 2^(n-1) <= a(n) <= n!, for n >= 1.
%F A180206 a(n) == 0 (mod 2) for n > 1. (End)
%e A180206 For n = 5, F(S) = 1 for every proper subset S of {1,2,3,4}, while F({1,2,3,4}) = 2. Thus a(5) = 14 + 2*2 = 18. - _Carlo Corti_, Nov 19 2026
%Y A180206 Cf. A180205, A180207, A180208, A180209, A180210, A180211, A180212, A229561.
%K A180206 nonn,changed
%O A180206 1,2
%A A180206 _R. H. Hardin_, Aug 15 2010
%E A180206 a(17)-a(26) from _Carlo Corti_, Nov 19 2026
